1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. f4 Bb4 4. Nf3 d6 5. Bc4 Nf6 6. d3 h6 7. O-O Bc5+ 8. Kh1
O-O 9. Na4 Bb6 10. Nxb6 axb6 11. fxe5 dxe5 12. Bd2 Bg4 13. Qe1 Nh7 14. Nh4 Bh5
15. Nf5 Ne7 16. Qg3 Ng6 17. Rf2 Ng5 18. Raf1 Kh7 {"The time for concluding the
tourney having arrived when Black made this move, the position was submitted
to the umpire [Steinitz], who adjudged the game to be White's. It is right to
say that Mr. Parratt's play throughout these games is far below his real
strength, owing to an almost total want of practice for some months." Sources:
Westminster Papers, 1 Apr 1874; Illustrated London News, 11 April 1874;
Huddersfield College Magazine, May 1874, p157.} 1-0

