1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. e3 Nf6 4. Nc3 Bb4 5. Bd3 Nc6 6. Nge2 ({White should here
have played} 6. Nf3 {which would have prevented the subsequent advance of his
opponent's e-pawn}) 6... e5 7. a3 dxc4 {(Black plays hereabouts very
vigorously)} 8. Bxc4 Bxc3+ 9. Nxc3 {(This move loses a clear pawn)} exd4 10.
Ne2 dxe3 11. Qxd8+ Nxd8 12. Bxe3 O-O 13. O-O Be6 14. Rac1 c6 15. Ng3 Nd5 16.
Bxd5 Bxd5 17. Bc5 Re8 18. Nf5 Ne6 19. Ne7+ Kh8 20. Nxd5 cxd5 21. Rfd1 b6 22.
Bd4 Rac8 23. Rxc8 Rxc8 24. g3 h6 ({Black should have played} 24... Rc4 {
winning easily}) 25. Kf1 Nxd4 26. Rxd4 Rc2 27. Rxd5 Rxb2 28. Rd7 a5 29. Rxf7
Rb3 30. a4 Rb4 31. Rb7 Kg8 32. h4 Rxa4 33. Rxb6 Ra1+ 34. Kg2 Rc1 35. Rb5 Ra1
36. Rb7 a4 37. Ra7 Kf8 38. h5 a3 39. Kf3 a2 40. Kf4 Ke8 41. Kf5 Rh1 42. Rxa2
Rxh5+ 43. Kg4 {and the game was given up as drawn (Source: Westminster Papers,
1 Apr 1874)} 1/2-1/2

