1. e4 b6 2. d4 Bb7 3. Nc3 {"This defence of the e-pawn is not at all
satisfactory because it blocks the c-pawn; 3.d5 followed by 4.c4 is good" 
(Zukertort/Wisker)} Nf6 4. Bd3 c5 5. Nf3 c4 6. e5 {"White has already the
inferior game" (Zukertort/Wisker)} cxd3 7. exf6 dxc2 {(Each side pursues his
own idea with great animation, but Black seems to get the best of the melee)}
8. Qxc2 exf6 9. O-O Be7 10. d5 O-O 11. Bf4 Bb4 12. Rad1 Na6 13. a3 Bxc3 14.
bxc3 Rc8 15. c4 b5 {"This advance is premature" (Zukertort/Wisker)} 16. Qb2
Rxc4 17. Qxb5 Rxf4 18. Qxb7 Ra4 19. Rd3 {"A blunder, which does not improve
White's prospects" (Zukertort/Wisker)} Nc5 20. Qb5 Ra5 21. Qc4 Nxd3 22. Qxd3
Qb6 23. d6 Qc6 24. Nh4 Rd5 25. Qg3 Re8 {(there is no reason why the queen
should not have taken the d-pawn)} ({"} 25... Qxd6 {was simple and sound" 
(Zukertort/Wisker)}) 26. Qg4 Rg5 27. Qd4 Re4 28. Qxa7 h6 ({"} 28... g6 {
was the proper move" (Zukertort/Wisker)}) 29. Qb8+ Kh7 30. Qb1 g6 31. Qb3 {
(The manoeuvres on both sides are rather amusing, though not destitute of
purpose)} Kg7 32. Nf3 Rc5 33. Nd2 Rg4 34. f3 Rd4 35. Qb2 {(The attack and
counter attack on both sides are kept up with vigour)} Rcd5 36. Ne4 Qc4 37. Rc1
Qxc1+ 38. Qxc1 Rd1+ 39. Qxd1 Rxd1+ 40. Kf2 Ra1 ({"} 40... f5 {would win at
once, giving Black a passed pawn" (Zukertort/Wisker)}) 41. a4 {"The intention
of this move surpasses the power of our comprehension" (Zukertort/Wisker)} Rxa4
42. Nc5 Rd4 43. Nxd7 Rxd6 44. Nc5 h5 45. Ne4 Rc6 46. Kg3 f5 47. Nf2 Rf6 ({"} 
47... g5 {would have saved immense time for the players, the recorder and the
readers. Black ought to win in about half-a-dozen moves, and he takes 40 to do
so. I hope to be excused analysing the remainder of the game" (Zukertort/
Wisker)}) 48. h4 Kh6 49. Nh3 Ra6 50. f4 f6 51. Kh2 Ra8 52. Kg3 Rg8 53. Kf3 Kg7
54. Ke3 Kf7 55. Nf2 g5 56. hxg5 {(PxP ambiguous)} fxg5 57. fxg5 Rxg5 58. Kf3
Kf6 59. Nh3 Rg8 60. g3 Ra8 61. Nf4 Ra3+ 62. Kg2 Kg5 63. Nh3+ Kh6 64. Nf4 Ra8
65. Nh3 Rg8 66. Kf3 Rf8 67. Nf4 Ra8 68. Kg2 Ra4 69. Kf3 Ra1 70. Kg2 Rb1 71. Kf2
Kg5 72. Kg2 Kg4 73. Ne2 Rb2 74. Kf2 Rxe2+ 75. Kxe2 Kxg3 {Source: Westminster
Papers, 1 Apr 1874 (longest game of the round, according to the Times report)}
0-1

