1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Qf6 {(This is not a good defence to the Ruy Lopez)}
4. O-O Bc5 5. c3 a6 6. Ba4 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. d4 exd4 9. Bg5 Qg6 10. Qd2 ({
A very weak move.} 10. Bd5 {was the correct line of play}) 10... h6 11. Bh4 Bh3
{(Useless. This B should have been played to g4 at once)} 12. Bg3 Bg4 13. cxd4
Bb6 14. a4 Bxf3 15. gxf3 Nxd4 16. Qd3 b4 17. Bc4 Qh5 18. Nd2 Nf6 19. e5 dxe5
20. Bxe5 Rd8 21. Bxa6 Ne6 22. Bb5+ Nd7 ({Black could here have won by playing} 
22... Kf8 {as White must then have lost a piece}) 23. Rae1 Qg5+ 24. Kh1 Qh4 25.
Bg3 Qf6 26. Re4 Qxb2 27. Be5 Qa3 28. Qc4 ({We believe White might have
retrieved his game at this point by} 28. Bxg7) 28... O-O 29. Bxd7 Rxd7 30. Ra1
Qd3 31. Qxd3 Rxd3 32. Nc4 Bxf2 33. Kg2 Bc5 34. Bg3 Ng5 35. Rf4 b3 36. Rf5 Bd4
37. Rb1 Re8 38. Be5 Bxe5 39. Rxe5 Rxe5 40. Nxe5 Rd2+ {(game ended at 9.15pm
having started at 6pm, acc. the Times report)} 41. Kg3 Ra2 42. Rxb3 Rxa4 43.
Rb7 f6 44. Ng6 c5 {Source: Westminster Papers, 1 Apr 1874} 0-1

